+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en">
+<meta charset="utf-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+<title>Arcium privacy policy</title>
+<style>
+  :root { color-scheme: light dark; font: 17px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
+  body { max-width: 42rem; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
+  h1 { font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; }
+  h2 { margin-top: 1.8rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
+  a { color: light-dark(#174ea6, #a8c7fa); text-underline-offset: .18em; }
+  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 4px; }
+  nav { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
+  .date { color: light-dark(#555, #bbb); }
+</style>
+<main>
+  <nav aria-label="Legal"><a href="privacy.html" aria-current="page">Privacy</a><a href="terms.html">Terms of use</a></nav>
+  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
+  <p class="date">Updated November 2, 2026</p>
+  <p>I'm Daniel, the operator of Arcium. Contact me at <a href="mailto:danielappsupport@gmail.com">danielappsupport@gmail.com</a>.</p>
+  <h2>Your browser data</h2>
+  <p>Arcium stores your history, bookmarks, saved tabs, settings and imported browser data on your device. It does not send that data to me. You can delete local data through the browser's settings.</p>
+  <h2>Connections you use</h2>
+  <p>Websites, search engines and extensions handle data under their own privacy policies. Network services receive your IP address and the information needed for your requests.</p>
+  <p>Optional Helium services provide extension downloads, component updates, filter lists and !bangs. You can manage them in Settings. They are operated by upstream Helium under <a href="https://helium.computer/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Helium's privacy policy</a>. A custom service instance has its own operator.</p>
+  <h2>Crash reports</h2>
+  <p>Crash reports go to Helium only when you choose to send a report or enable automatic reporting. They can contain sensitive data from browser memory. Crash reporting has a separate control in Settings.</p>
+  <h2>If you contact me</h2>
+  <p>I use the messages and attachments you send to provide support and fix problems. Email is handled by Google under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">its privacy policy</a>. I keep support information only as long as needed for those purposes or legal obligations. I don't sell it.</p>
+  <p>Email me to request access, correction or deletion of information you've sent me, or to ask a privacy question. I'll respond as required by applicable law. Changes to this policy ship with new versions of Arcium.</p>
+</main>
+</html>
